    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d2">

                <pb facs="0057" n="3" sameAs="frus:frus1944Quebec/pg3"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt
                        to Prime Minister Churchill</hi><anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d2-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-03-20">20 March 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Number 506. Personal and secret. From the President for the Former Naval Person.</p>
                <p>I am very angry with myself. The old attack of grippe having hung on and on,
                    leaving me with an intermittent temperature, Ross<anchor n="2" xml:id="d2-f2"/>
                    decided about a week ago that it is necessary for me to take a complete rest <pb
                        facs="0058" n="4" xml:id="pg4"/> of about two or three weeks in a suitable
                    climate which I am definitely planning to do beginning at the end of this month.
                    I see no way out and I am furious.</p>
                <p>It will therefore be impossible for me to get to a staff meeting in early April.
                    I believe that such a meeting on the Teheran scale in early April would be most
                    useful and if you agree I will send my Chiefs of Staff to Bermuda for that
                    purpose at any time that suits your convenience.</p>
                <p>I am glad you feel hardened about <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">Overlord</hi>. Its accomplishment may
                    synchronize with a real Russian break-through.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Roosevelt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d2-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d2-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to the United States Naval Attaché, London, via Navy channels.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d2-f2" n="2" xml:id="d2-f2-content">
                <p>Vice Admiral Ross T. McIntire, Roosevelt’s physician.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
